ntresor completing the wall, restoring the pile of bones over it, and declaring that no one has disturbed the site in fifty years.\"\n    28→    }\n    29→  ],\n    30→  \"characters\": [\n    31→    {\n    32→      \"id\": \"char_amontillado_1b7d65f7\",\n    33→      \"canonical_name\": \"Amontillado\",\n    34→      \"aliases\": [],\n    35→      \"role\": null,\n    36→      \"appearance\": null,\n    37→      \"personality\": null,\n    38→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    39→      \"descriptions\": [\n    40→        {\n    41→          \"text\": \"The narrator is a calculated and vengeful individual who manipulates another man, Fortunato, under the pretense of a shared interest in wine, ultimately leading him to his death. Throughout the narrative, the narrator maintains a calm, deceptive demeanor while orchestrating a premeditated murder, revealing his deep-seated malice and lack of remorse through his actions and internal monologue.\",\n    42→          \"source_position\": 2046,\n    43→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    44→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    45→        }\n    46→      ],\n    47→      \"relationships\": {},\n    48→      \"evidence\": [],\n    49→      \"voice_notes\": null,\n    50→      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n    51→      \"mention_count\": 16,\n    52→      \"confidence\": \"low\",\n    53→      \"is_narrator\": false,\n    54→      \"narrative_role\": null\n    55→    },\n    56→    {\n    57→      \"id\": \"char_fortunato_b564181f\",\n    58→      \"canonical_name\": \"Fortunato\",\n    59→      \"aliases\": [],\n    60→      \"role\": null,\n    61→      \"appearance\": null,\n    62→      \"personality\": null,\n    63→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    64→      \"descriptions\": [\n    65→        {\n    66→          \"text\": \"Fortunato is a man whose pride in his expertise in wine leads to his downfall. He is portrayed as intoxicated, trusting, and ultimately helpless as he is lured into a trap by M