tresor lures the drunken, costumed Fortunato—wearing a jingling motley outfit—into the damp, bone-strewn catacombs beneath his palazzo under the pretense of tasting a rare pipe of Amontillado. As they descend through the vaults, Montresor feigns concern for Fortunato’s cough, offering wine to ease his discomfort, while subtly guiding him deeper into the family crypts. Once in a secluded niche lined with human remains, Montresor chains Fortunato to the wall and begins sealing him alive behind a brick wall, methodically building it tier by tier as Fortunato’s initial laughter turns to desperate pleas and finally silence. The chapter ends with Montresor completing the wall, restoring the pile of bones over it, and declaring that no one has disturbed the site in fifty years.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_amontillado_1b7d65f7\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"Amontillado\",\n      \"aliases\": [],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"The narrator is a calculated and vengeful individual who manipulates another man, Fortunato, under the pretense of a shared interest in wine, ultimately leading him to his death. Throughout the narrative, the narrator maintains a calm, deceptive demeanor while orchestrating a premeditated murder, revealing his deep-seated malice and lack of remorse through his actions and internal monologue.\",\n          \"source_position\": 2046,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"voice_notes\": null,\n      \"first_appearance_chapter\": 1,\n      \"mention_count\": 16,\n      \"confidence\": \"low\",\n      \"is_narrator\": false,\n      \"narrative_role\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_fortunato_b564181f\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"Fortunato\"